{ ================================================================================
  S3_S - VOLATILITY SQUEEZE SHORT STRATEGY
  Signal Name : S3_VolSqueezeShort
  MC Load Name: STRATEGY_GEN_S3_VolSqueezeShort
  Version     : v1.2  (2026-06-24 - BUGFIX cooldown predicate; Layer 2 SP unchanged)
  Symbol      : TXF1 (Taiwan Stock Index Futures Front Month)
  Platform    : MultiCharts 12 PowerLanguage x64
  Timeframe   : Data1 = 60M (sole feed, no multi-TF)
  Class       : Volatility Regime (C class) - Short only (Rule R-6 split)
  Direction   : Short only
  Allocation  : TBD (post W4 Walk-Forward)

  CREATED 2026-06-23
    From OFFICIAL_ROADMAP.md (docs/policies/OFFICIAL_ROADMAP.md)
    Source spec: strategies/research/archive/batch01_S2-S5/TXF1_Strategies_Batch01.md S3 VolSqueeze
    R-6 split (2026-06-22): original bi-directional -> Sx_L pure long + Sx_S pure short
    Order rule: L first, S second (TXF1 2020-2026 bullish regime)
    This file is the S (short) version; S3_L VolSqueezeLong already promoted to live_simulation.

  STAGE-1 DESIGN DECISIONS (2026-06-23 user-ruled):
    1. Period: 60M (same as S3_L) - keeps R-6 symmetric for clean comparison.
    2. Short-side params NOT mirrored from S3_L because short panic structure differs:
       - Long trend: slow grind, far TP (ATR x 8)
       - Short panic: fast drop then range, near TP (ATR x 3.5)
       - Long holds 70 bars; short holds 35 bars max
       - Long Mid exit 3 bars; short 2 bars (faster bounce reaction)
    3. Cooldown_Days = 0 (user ruling: SL controls per-trade risk, no daily limit)
       - W3 will A/B test (0 vs 1) to verify
    4. Short-side variant: SetStopLoss guard = MP >= 0 (per Rule #12 short variant)
    5. Frozen SL: v_SL_Level = EntryPrice + v_Frozen_SL_Dist (above entry)
    6. All other compliance modules byte-identical to S3_L.

  CHANGELOG:
    v1.2 (2026-06-24): BUGFIX - Section 8 cooldown reset predicate corrected
         Symptom: A/B test (Cool=0 vs Cool=1) returned 100 pct identical results
                  (185 trades both, same Net/PF/MDD/all metrics), proving the
                  cooldown gate was effectively non-functional.
         Root cause: Section 8 reset required BOTH "Date <> v_LastExit_Date"
                     AND "DateDiff >= Cooldown_Days" - the first clause is
                     redundant and creates a contradiction:
                       Cool=0 same day: diff=0 OK, but Date==LastExit fails
                         -> cooldown stays True forever, NEVER allows reset
                       Cool=1 same day: diff=0<1 anyway
                       Both branches behave identically (cool effectively dead).
         Fix: removed "Date <> v_LastExit_Date" clause; pure DateDiff>=Cooldown:
                Cool=0 -> diff>=0 always True -> resets every bar -> same-day OK
                Cool=1 -> diff>=1 -> next-day only -> same-day blocked
         Action: re-run A/B (Cool=0 baseline + Cool=1 variant) to confirm fix.

    v1.1 (2026-06-24): add Layer 2 - Trailing StopProfit (per annotated.md 5-layer ruling)
         Driver: user identified short-side asymmetry - short panic reverses faster
         than long pullback, so peak-profit protection earlier (vs L1 SP) is needed.
         New inputs:
           SP_Trigger_ATRMult ( 1.5 )  - arm SP when peak profit >= ATR * 1.5
           SP_Retain_Pct      ( 70  )  - retain 70% of peak (tolerate 30% giveback)
         New label: SX_VS_SP (mutually exclusive with SX_VS_SL)
         Logic:
           1. Track v_Peak_Profit_Pts = max(EntryPrice - Low) over hold
           2. Arm v_SP_Armed when peak >= ATR * SP_Trigger_ATRMult (irreversible)
           3. Compute v_SP_Floor_Price = EntryPrice - (peak * SP_Retain_Pct / 100)
           4. While armed: SL order replaced by SP order at floor price
           5. Reset all SP state when flat
         Versus L1 SP (45% retain):
           S3_S uses 70% retain because short bounces are sharper than long pullbacks.
         Per Lesson L24: this is ATR-based dynamic protection, NOT event filter.

    v1.0 (2026-06-23): initial release, R-6 short mirror with 4 params customized:
         - TargetATRMult  8.0 -> 3.5   (short panic = fast drop, near TP)
         - MaxBars        70  -> 35    (short holds shorter)
         - MidExit_MinBars 3  -> 2     (faster bounce reaction)
         - Cooldown_Days  1   -> 0     (user ruling: no daily limit)
         All other inputs mirror S3_L v1.1 Phase 3 best:
         BBLen=45, BBStd=2.0, BWLookback=120, BWPctile=30, ATR_Len=14, StopATRMult=2.75

  ALPHA THESIS:
    Bollinger BandWidth (BBW) compressed to 30-percentile of past 120 periods
    = volatility squeeze, statistically anticipates expansion.
    Short entry: Squeeze condition + Close < Lower Band (downward breakout).
    Theory: vol cycle expansion -> directional follow-through (downward variant).

    Macro shock catalysts for TXF1 are asymmetric: FOMC tightening, Trump tariffs,
    US limit down, geopolitical war, BoJ surprise = predominantly DOWNSIDE catalysts.
    Short panic is faster and more violent than long FOMO (panic > FOMO).
    But TXF1 2020-2026 is bullish regime overall, so:
      - Sample expected: 50-100 trades / 6yr (vs S3_L 134)
      - Single Sharpe expected: < 0.5 (vs S3_L 1.02)
      - PORTFOLIO Sharpe with S3_L pairing: expected > 1.2
    Hedge value (R-6 directional pair) > single-sleeve Sharpe per Lesson L24.

  PARAMETERIZATION:
    All numeric thresholds are PowerLanguage inputs - none hardcoded.
    v1.0 defaults = 4 short-customized + 8 mirrored from S3_L Phase 3 best.
    W3 baseline backtest will A/B test Cooldown_Days (0 vs 1).
    W4 Walk-Forward IS 2y / OOS 6m / step 6m (same setup as S3_L).

  LESSON CHECK (mandatory header reminders):
    1. CLOSED TIME INTERVALS (Rule MC_Time_24hr):
       60M bars - holiday tail detection at Time<=500 within day boundary;
       all Time>=X conditions paired with state guards OR explicit Time<=Y.
    2. FILTER REDUNDANCY CHECK (Rule Filter_Redundancy):
       BBW + Close<Lower = 2 conditions, orthogonal. Squeeze = state, Close = trigger.
    3. VOLUME SIGNAL: not used (consistent with S3_L, archive S3 also didn't use volume).

  CONSTITUTION COMPLIANCE (mandatory per CLAUDE.md Rule #11/#12/#13/#14):
    Rule #11 Settlement_Flat (7 elements): present in Priority 0.
    Rule #12 P3b SetStopLoss: single call before entry block,
             guarded by MarketPosition >= 0 (SHORT variant).
    Rule #13 10-dim eval before live_simulation: deferred to W5 gate.
    Rule #14 OFFICIAL_ROADMAP alignment: S3_S is next per official sequence after S3_L.
    Rule #15 ASCII-only (all .pla source): 100% ASCII.

  LABEL CONVENTIONS (Short-only):
    SE_VS_Entry        short entry
    SX_VS_Kill         manual kill switch (P0-1)
    SX_VS_RegistryEnd  registry expired (P0-2)
    SX_VS_HolFlat      holiday tail flat (P0-3)
    SX_VS_Settlement   settlement day flat (P0-4)
    SX_VS_TP           target profit (Layer 4)
    SX_VS_Mid          mid-band exit / thesis fail (Layer 3)
    SX_VS_TimeStop     time exit (Layer 5)
    SX_VS_SP           trailing stop profit / breakeven floor (Layer 2, NEW v1.1)
    SX_VS_SL           initial stop loss (Layer 1, fallback when SP not armed)
    No Long labels (R-6 split produced separate S3_L file).

  STATUS: v1.0 ready for MC12 baseline backtest (W3 phase).
          Pending: W3 baseline, W4 WFA, W5 10-dim eval.
================================================================================ }

[IntrabarOrderGeneration = false]


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 1 - INPUTS
  v1.0 defaults: 4 short-customized + 8 mirrored from S3_L Phase 3 best.
  All inputs MC12-optimizable.
  ============================================================ }

inputs:
    { ===== Bollinger Bands (core squeeze detection - mirrored from S3_L) ===== }
    BBLen                     ( 45    ),   { mirror S3_L Phase 3 best }
    BBStd                     ( 2.0   ),   { mirror }
    BWLookback                ( 120   ),   { mirror }
    BWPctile                  ( 30    ),   { mirror }

    { ===== ATR (stop / target anchor - SL mirrored, TP customized for short) ===== }
    ATR_Len                   ( 14    ),   { mirror }
    StopATRMult               ( 2.75  ),   { mirror - SL symmetric }
    TargetATRMult             ( 3.5   ),   { CUSTOMIZED - short panic fast drop, near TP }

    { ===== Exit timing (CUSTOMIZED for short structure) ===== }
    MaxBars                   ( 35    ),   { CUSTOMIZED - short holds shorter (vs S3_L 70) }
    UseMidExit                ( True  ),   { mid-band exit on/off }
    MidExit_MinBars           ( 2     ),   { CUSTOMIZED - faster bounce reaction (vs S3_L 3) }

    { ===== Layer 2: Trailing StopProfit (v1.1 NEW, short-only) ===== }
    SP_Trigger_ATRMult        ( 1.5   ),   { NEW v1.1: arm SP when peak profit >= ATR * 1.5 }
    SP_Retain_Pct             ( 70    ),   { NEW v1.1: retain 70 pct of peak (tolerate 30 pct giveback) }

    { ===== Same-day cooldown (CUSTOMIZED per user ruling) ===== }
    Cooldown_Days             ( 0     ),   { CUSTOMIZED - no daily limit (vs S3_L 1); W3 A/B }

    { ===== Priority 0 Protection (Rule #11 / #12 - mirrored from S3_L) ===== }
    Holiday_Flat_Time         ( 415   ),   { 60M grid -> fire 04:15 holiday tail }
    Registry_Valid_Until      ( 1270101 ), { TAIFEX-verified horizon; bump each Q4 }
    Manual_Kill_Switch        ( False ),
    Settlement_Flat_Time      ( 1230  );   { 1hr buffer before 13:30 settlement }


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 2 - VARIABLES
  ============================================================ }

variables:
    { ===== Bollinger Bands ===== }
    v_MidBand                ( 0     ),
    v_UpperBand              ( 0     ),
    v_LowerBand              ( 0     ),
    v_BandWidth              ( 0     ),
    v_BWRank                 ( 0     ),
    v_BWCount                ( 0     ),
    v_Squeeze                ( False ),

    { ===== ATR ===== }
    v_ATR                    ( 0     ),
    v_StopDist               ( 0     ),
    v_TargetDist             ( 0     ),

    { ===== Trade state ===== }
    v_EntryBar               ( 0     ),
    v_Prev_MP                ( 0     ),

    { ===== Frozen SL (Rule #12 backup, Short variant) ===== }
    v_SL_Locked              ( False ),
    v_Frozen_ATR             ( 0     ),
    v_Frozen_SL_Dist         ( 0     ),
    v_SL_Level               ( 0     ),

    { ===== Layer 2 SP state (v1.1 NEW) ===== }
    v_SP_Armed               ( False ),
    v_Peak_Profit_Pts        ( 0     ),
    v_SP_Floor_Price         ( 0     ),

    { ===== Cooldown ===== }
    v_LastExit_Date          ( 0     ),
    v_Cooldown_Active        ( False ),

    { ===== Priority 0 protection state ===== }
    v_Holiday_Block          ( False ),
    v_Registry_Expired       ( False ),
    v_Settlement_Day         ( False ),
    Registry_Warn_ID         ( -1    ),
    hidx                     ( 0     ),
    v_i                      ( 0     ),
    ExitFired                ( 0     );


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 3 - ARRAYS
  Holiday_Tail: shared 63-entry TAIFEX registry (byte-identical to L1-L5/S1/S3/S3_L).
  ============================================================ }

arrays:
    Holiday_Tail[80]( 0 );


